 ShowCellLabel->False,ExpressionUUID->"45fc2c0b-6c68-408e-b09c-d4d0c1b754d1"],

Cell["3. Adding a second equation: Payne-Whitham", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"63baea70-a75e-498b-969f-47bbe29bfa5a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A weakness of the LWR model is that velocity is always the instantaneous \
equilibrium value on the fundamental diagram \[LongDash] drivers adapt \
infinitely fast. Real drivers take a second or two to react, and they \
anticipate the state of traffic ahead. Payne (1971) and Whitham (1974) \
independently proposed a second equation \[LongDash] a momentum equation \
\[LongDash] in which velocity relaxes with time constant ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["\[Tau]", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "bac4b92d-5095-49fe-95cb-52fed9defc47"],
 " towards its equilibrium ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["V", "e"], "(", "\[Rho]", ")"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "6a1d778a-dd47-4ffe-8c25-6bfb7020586f"],
 " and is pushed by a pressure-like term ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    SubscriptBox["c", "0"], "2"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "28fc129b-8981-4cf5-8f7d-749fe98dbd9a"],
 " representing anticipation:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0f7c39ac-94f0-46d6-afe6-88b07f2f436a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{"\[PartialD]", "v"}], 
     RowBox[{"\[PartialD]", "t"}]], "+", "v", 
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{"\[PartialD]", "v"}], 
     RowBox[{"\[PartialD]", "x"}]]}], 
   FractionBox[
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox["V", "e"], "(", "\[Rho]", ")"}], "-", "v"}], "\[Tau]"], "-", 
   FractionBox[
    SuperscriptBox[
     SubscriptBox["c", "0"], "2"], "\[Rho]"], 
   FractionBox[
    RowBox[{"\[PartialD]", "\[Rho]"}], 
    RowBox[{"\[PartialD]", "x"}]]}], TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",
 TextAlignment->Center,
 FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->"d4934066-9430-4735-ba59-f2de521fa3d4"],

Cell["\<\
coupled to the same continuity equation as LWR. The system is now \
second-order and supports stop-and-go waves: velocity is no longer slaved to \
density. In our numerical experiment we seed a congested block on an \
otherwise moderate-density corridor \[LongDash] the kind of configuration you \
get at an on-ramp merge \[LongDash] and watch the oscillatory structure \
develop.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"25326605-6fe0-4709-ab88-7b9d0581884c"],

