Cell["11. The full case study: Aberdeen from OpenStreetMap", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"49e57eb1-0b0b-484c-a1a0-e21cf68a7368"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "All the ingredients above stitch together to produce a realistic \
multi-agent simulation of the full Aberdeen drivable road network. The \
network is parsed from an Overpass API JSON extract (council-area-wide query) \
by filtering for drivable ",
 StyleBox["highway=*",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " tags and splitting each way at intersection nodes, which leaves an 11\
\[ThinSpace]925-node, 26\[ThinSpace]453-edge directed graph after restricting \
to the largest strongly-connected component. 151 OSM-tagged traffic-signal \
junctions get a fixed-time controller with a 60\[ThinSpace]s cycle, 4\
\[ThinSpace]s amber, and a randomised offset. ~1000 edges tagged ",
 StyleBox["junction=roundabout",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " enforce gap acceptance via a TRL\\[ThinSpace]281-style critical headway."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"24281f45-5f24-4d88-97f7-bccae084f18c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Every vehicle carries a full IDM car-following state (a=2, b=3, s0=2, \
T=1.2, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\[Delta]", "=", "4"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "87187b2a-2e80-4fbd-8a69-22355d33ade9"],
 ", with the velocity-difference term). Origin-destination pairs are sampled \
by node degree so trips cluster at major intersections. Routes are computed \
on a graph whose edge weights are length times a per-highway-class factor \
(0.5 for motorway, 1.2 for residential, \[Ellipsis]) times a frozen per-edge \
random factor in [0.8, 1.5], giving genuine route diversity without \
rebuilding the graph on every call. Entries are staggered over the first 60\
\[ThinSpace]s, and at each junction there is a 10% chance of a probabilistic \
detour. Within 15\[ThinSpace]m of the stop line a red signal or a blocked \
roundabout caps the vehicle's speed-limit-for-IDM at a distance-proportional \
value, causing the IDM to decelerate naturally towards the stop."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b2affe8f-493f-4c5a-9ced-5e24005767b4"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Get", "[", "\"\<IntersectionControl.wl\>\"", "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Get", "[", "\"\<AberdeenFullCity.wl\>\"", "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"net", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"AberdeenFullCity`LoadFullAberdeen", "[", "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"sim", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"AberdeenFullCity`SimulateFullAberdeen", "[", 
    RowBox[{"net", ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<nVehicles\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "600"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<nFrames\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "120"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<T\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "360"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"AberdeenFullCity`PlotFullAberdeen", "[", 
   RowBox[{"sim", ",", " ", "\"\<aberdeen_full.png\>\""}], "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"AberdeenFullCity`AnimateFullAberdeen", "[", 
   RowBox[{"sim", ",", " ", "\"\<aberdeen_full.gif\>\""}], "]"}], 
  ";"}]}], "Input",ExpressionUUID->"84912b94-80db-4376-b80b-b3c8bf1bd3f4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "On an M-class laptop this pipeline takes about 30\[ThinSpace]s for the \
simulation and a minute for the GIF export. The final frame at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"t", "=", 
    RowBox[{"360", " ", "s"}]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "afbdb78e-1564-498f-ac99-a5bd424f2c1a"],
 " shows the Aberdeen Western Peripheral Route on the outer ring, heavy flows \
along the A90 down the east coast and into the city, and congestion at the \
expected pinch points."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5d717e96-099f-42c3-b348-820deeaa5def"],

